# Range Rover P38A, 1994-2001.
#
# The second-generation Range Rover: 4,714 mm long, 1,890 mm wide, 1,803 mm high,
# 2,746 mm wheelbase; 4.0 and 4.6 V8 and a 2.5 diesel. Upright boxy estate with a
# floating roof, horizontal shoulder line and split tailgate.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Range_Rover#Second_generation_(1994)
#
# Colours: Epsom Green, Java Black, Blenheim Silver and Oxford Blue are period
# Range Rover finishes.
#
# Weight: 40 in total (green 14, black 10, silver 10, blue 6) — the Range Rover
# family was the largest class-4 parc of the 1990s (about 60,000 licensed in
# 1994, all generations), with the P38 a growing share.
#
# Speed 190 km/h; comfort 140/390 (line). Classes 2,3,4.
# Dates: 1994-2001 with a road tail to about 2012.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/range-rover-p38.blend. References:
# citycars/references/range-rover-p38/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=RangeRoverP38(EpsomGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=14
intro_year=1994
intro_month=9
retire_year=2012
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=140
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=390

